\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 Since the beginning of this year there have been advances in glTF. Please provide a summary.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \cb4 \strokec5 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb1 \
\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 Since the beginning of 2026, the glTF ecosystem has seen some massive leaps forward, primarily focused on bridging the gap between traditional 3D geometry and photorealistic real-world scanning.  \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa340\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Here is a summary of the most significant advances and announcements in the glTF space so far this year:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs40 \cf2 1. Standardization of 3D Gaussian Splatting\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 The absolute biggest news in early 2026 is the Khronos Group\'92s release candidate for the 
\f2\fs22\fsmilli11250 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 KHR_gaussian_splatting
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  extension (announced in February). Gaussian splatting has revolutionized how we capture and render real-world environments, and now it is being natively integrated into glTF.  \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \
\cb3 + 1\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa340\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f3\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How it works:
\f0\b0  The extension modifies the glTF 2.0 mesh primitive to store Gaussian splat datasets (position, orientation, scale, color, and opacity) instead of traditional triangles.  \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Why it matters:
\f0\b0  This allows highly detailed, photorealistic 3D captures of homes, neighborhoods, or specific rooms to be easily shared and loaded on the web using existing glTF pipelines.  \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\ls4\ilvl0
\f3\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Graceful Fallback:
\f0\b0  If a user's device or browser viewer doesn't support Gaussian splats, the glTF file will gracefully fall back to displaying a standard point cloud.  \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs40 \cf2 2. Extreme Compression via SPZ\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 Alongside the Gaussian splatting extension, Khronos has heavily collaborated with spatial computing leaders like Niantic, Cesium, and Esri to integrate 
\f3\b SPZ compression
\f0\b0  into the standard.  \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 Let's Data Science\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa340\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Because Gaussian splats can be incredibly data-heavy, SPZ compression drastically reduces the file footprint (up to 90% smaller compared to older formats like 
\f2\fs22\fsmilli11250 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 .ply
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 ), making it actually feasible to stream these photorealistic assets to web browsers and mobile devices quickly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs40 \cf2 3. Push for Declarative Interactivity\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 There is a growing movement to embed 
\f3\b interaction metadata
\f0\b0  directly into the 
\f2\fs22\fsmilli11250 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 .glTF
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  file. Proposals circulating this year (such as those tied to Google Summer of Code 2026 for Blender) aim to let 3D artists declare interaction events\'97like clicks, hovers, and scrolls\'97before the model is even exported.  \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 Blender Devtalk\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa340\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Instead of a web developer having to write custom JavaScript to figure out what happens when a user clicks an ADU's front door, the 
\f2\fs22\fsmilli11250 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 .glTF
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  file itself would carry metadata saying, "When this object is clicked, play the 'OpenDoor' animation." This will eventually make building interactive configurators much easier.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f4\fs40 \cf2 4. The Khronos EIO Subgroup Launch\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 In April 2026, recognizing that glTF is being pushed into heavier enterprise use cases (like digital twins, architectural tech, and e-commerce), the Khronos 3D Formats Working Group launched the 
\f3\b Education, Insights, and Outreach (EIO) Subgroup
\f0\b0 .  \
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa340\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Their mandate is to bridge the gap between the highly technical glTF specifications and practical developer implementations. They are actively rolling out new technical blogs, webinars, and real-world guides to help developers optimize their 3D web pipelines.  \uc0\u8232 
\f6\fs30 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 The Khronos Group\cb1 \uc0\u8232 
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\b \cf2 The Takeaway for Your ADU Project:
\f0\b0 \
If you ever plan to move beyond standardized 3D models and start showing homeowners photorealistic scans of what an ADU looks like in an actual backyard context, the 2026 Gaussian Splatting extensions mean you will be able to do so while sticking strictly to the 
\f2\fs22\fsmilli11250 \cf6 \cb3 \strokec6 .glTF
\f0\fs34 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2  format you are already using.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

